    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.rescale_layout - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.rescale_layout.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.rescale_layout()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Center and resize a layout that's already been computed.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.rescale_layout()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Center and resize a layout that's already been computed.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.rescale_layout()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Center and resize a layout that's already been computed.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nCenter and resize a layout that's already been computed.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L7391-L7504){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.rescale_layout(\n    scale=1.0,\n    center=(0.0, 0.0),\n    pos=\"pos\",\n    attr_name=None,\n    return_dict=False,\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Rescale a layout](../assets/graphs/rescale-layout.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"A four-node cycle placed by hand: nodes 1 to 4 at (0, 0), (4, 8), (12, 8) and (16, 0), with a small cross at their mean (8, 4). After rescale_layout() the same shape is centered on the origin and fits the dashed square from -1 to 1: the nodes move to (-1, -0.5), (-0.5, 0.5), (0.5, 0.5) and (1, -0.5), shown in accent.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nShifts the positions so their mean sits at `center=`, then scales them evenly (keeping\nthe drawing's shape) so the coordinate farthest from it is `scale=` away along `x` or\n`y`. Every `layout_*()` method does this to its own result; use this to bring positions\nfrom elsewhere (a file, another library, hand placement, or a layout run with\n`scale=None`) into the same frame, for example to draw two layouts side by side. With a\nsingle node, or all nodes at one point, the positions are only moved. Matches\nNetworkX's `rescale_layout_dict()` (and `rescale_layout()` on an array of positions)\nwith the result shifted to `center=`.\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[scale]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [float]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[1.0]{.fl}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The largest distance from `center=` along either axis. Default is `1.0`.\n\n<code>[center]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [tuple[float, float]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [(0.0, 0.0)]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Where the positions' mean goes, as `(x, y)`. Default is the origin.\n\n<code>[pos]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Union[str, dict]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;pos&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   The positions to rescale: the name of a node attribute holding `(x, y)` pairs\n    (default `\"pos\"`, where the `layout_*()` methods store them) or a\n    `{node: (x, y)}` dictionary keyed by node ID or label. Only the nodes that have a\n    position are rescaled.\n\n<code>[attr_name]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Node attribute to store the new positions in. If `None` (default), the attribute\n    named by `pos=` (so it's rescaled in place), or `\"pos\"` when `pos=` is a dictionary.\n\n<code>[return_dict]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[False]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True`, returns a dictionary instead of self. If `False` (default), stores the\n    positions on the nodes and returns self for chaining.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Union[dict[int, tuple[float, float]], Graph]]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `return_dict=` is `True`: dictionary mapping node IDs to `(x, y)` tuples. If\n    `return_dict=` is `False` (default): returns self for method chaining.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `scale=` is not a positive number, `center=` is not a pair of numbers, no node\n    has the `pos=` attribute, or a position is not a pair of finite numbers.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~layout_random`) \n\n:   Place nodes at random.\n\n[](`~set_node_attrs`) \n\n:   Store values on nodes.\n\n[](`~plot`) \n\n:   Draw the graph using stored positions.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nPositions placed by hand are centered on the origin and fit into the unit square:\n\n::: {#1736ec86 .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_path_graph(3)\n\ngraph.rescale_layout(\n    pos={1: (0, 0), 2: (10, 5), 3: (20, 10)}, return_dict=True\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n{1: (-1.0, -0.5), 2: (0.0, 0.0), 3: (1.0, 0.5)}\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Two floors side by side\n\nThe rooms of a two-story office have positions on the plan, in meters, with the second floor\ndrawn above the first. Rescaling each floor's positions separately, with its own `center=`,\nputs the floors side by side instead:\n\n::: {#b8e87786 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\noffices = ec.offices()\npos = offices.get_node_attrs(\"pos\")\nfloor = offices.get_node_attrs(\"floor\")\n\n\ndef floor_plan(level, center):\n    rooms = {n: p for n, p in pos.items() if floor[n] == level}\n    return offices.rescale_layout(\n        pos=rooms, center=center, return_dict=True\n    )\n\n\nside = floor_plan(1, (-1.25, 0)) | floor_plan(2, (1.25, 0))\noffices.set_node_attrs(\"side\", side)\n\noffices.plot(\n    layout=\"side\", color_by=\"floor\", label_by=\"label\", height=320\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21